      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Number of Permutations of Objects Chosen From a Group Fewer Than Ten",
      "problem": "Ashley has $5$ tasks. She decides to do one on Thursday and another on Friday. How many different choices of the two tasks does Ashley have?",
      "worked_solution": "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $5$ tasks to choose from, so $n=5.$ We want to select $2$ of those for Ashley to do, so we have $r=2.$ \n\nTherefore, the number of different choices is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{5}{P}_{2} & =\\frac{5!}{(5-2)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{5!}{3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 4\\cdot \\cancel{3!}}{\\cancel{3!}} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
